 "question": "Does a CPU-only kinematic pre-check of the copied human path (IK error + table/tray penetration, no rollout) flag the demo/robot pairs whose style was infeasible in simulation, and pass the feasible ones?",
 "thresholds": {
  "IK_ERR_MAX_M": 0.02,
  "PENETRATION_MAX_M": 0.005
 },
 "threshold_rationale": "2 cm = half the 4 cm block (a grasp commanded further away cannot close on it); 5 mm = well beyond MuJoCo's resting-contact overlap (~1 mm). Fixed before any validation case was run (code was smoke-tested on synthetic demos 7 and 8 only, which are not cases).",
 "method": "transfergap/sim/feasibility.py: retargeted path (demo.style.robot_path) for the nominal block and the 4 corners of the seed jitter square; converged DLS IK per point (controller objective, tool down, rot weight 0.6), warm-started; mj_collision of robot geoms vs table/tray at each IK pose; carried block bottom vs surface on the carry leg. Verdict uses reach/carry/retreat (the align move from home is robot-side, reported only). G1: g1/plan_reach.plan_style IK error with the frozen g1_contact_v1 calibration args (IK only, no collision check).",
 "labels": "feasible / infeasible from the earlier simulated outcomes (source folder per case). safe_path_v2 cases: feasible if >= 45/60 held-out with their stack, else ambiguous (not scored). 'prediction' cases have no simulated ground truth and are not scored.",
